  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.0: IEEE 754 float family — new opt-in dialect setting FloatFamilySupport.Float32AndFloat64 adds the `float32` type (System.Single) and the `float64` alias for `real`; real literals and math built-ins (`/`, sqrt, sin, ...) become generic over [float32..real] and resolve to float32 in float32 context. Added int8 (sbyte) type support. Fixed type inference for inline struct arrays with optional narrowing numeric fields (e.g. `arr:{v:float32?}[] = [{v=1.5}, {v=none}]`). Internal function-registry rework: faster overload lookup without per-call string allocation.",
